Dear INLA experts,

I am trying to understand how to implement multivariate mixed models in INLA. Consider this simplified example:

On the left hand side of the model, we have a presence (1) absence (0) matrix with 10 columns and 10,000 rows. Each column describes whether an event occured or not. We expect certain columns to be highly correlated with one another.

On the right hand side we have a random intercept f(id, model = "iid) describing a shared structure across the 10 responses.

>From this model, we want to extract a 10*10 matrix describing the correlation between  each response, whilst accounting for the "iid" structure. Can this be done in INLA?

Cheers, Tom UoSheffield

