Hi Denis,

I have a follow-up question: can we apply the same approach for Weibull survival analysis with age as a time-varying covariate? In this case, age is defined as the age at the occurrence of an event, death, emigration, or the end of the follow-up period. Your insights on this matter would be greatly appreciated.

Thank you for your time.

